STEP-05 — RUNTIME CONSTRUCTION ORDER

Purpose: Define the deterministic engineering build sequence for the Capability Environment. Every implementation artifact is built in dependency order, validated, and frozen before the next level begins.

1. Engineering Philosophy

The Capability Environment is not implemented by writing files in arbitrary order.

It is assembled as a deterministic runtime.

Every implementation unit has prerequisites.

No implementation shall bypass its dependency chain.

The construction order itself becomes part of the architecture.

2. Construction Principles

Every build level must satisfy:

Previous level is complete.
Previous level passes compilation.
Previous level passes validation.
Previous level exposes stable public APIs.
Previous level is frozen before the next level begins.

No downstream implementation may modify upstream contracts.

